Supported  options: command can be one of the following: configu‐
ration file realm If is given, then the given, configured, or de‐
fault log file will be truncated and will  start  at  version  1.
This  forces  full propagations to all slave KDCs.  Otherwise the
log will be truncated but some  entries  will  be  preserved,  as
specified  by  the and/or options.  The largest number of entries
that are available and fit in the given option will be used.  The
option defaults to the parameter in the configuration.   configu‐
ration file realm Print out all entries in the given, configured,
or  default  log  file to standard output.  If the option is used
then don’t lock the iprop log file.  If the option is used,  then
print  the  entries in reverse order (this can be useful when the
log is very large).  start replay with this  version  end  replay
with  this  version  configuration  file realm Replay the changes
from specified entries (or all  if  none  is  specified)  in  the
given,  configured,  or default transaction log file to the data‐
base.  configuration file realm prints the version  of  the  last
record  in each of the given log files, or the configured, or the
default log file if none is given.  configuration file realm Sig‐
nals the ipropd‐master daemon to send updates  to  slaves.   Nor‐
mally  kadmin  does this every time it writes to the database, so
this should rarely be needed.
